## What was implemented

- `apps/api/src/domain/files/seven-source-plan.ts` -- uc-22-3 R3 step 2's seven-row file
  contract table, keyed by F40's `MaterializationSourceType` (survey / conversation /
  interview / workshop / research / canvas / generated), plus the `ArtifactSource` tag
  each source's rows are written under (documented workaround for `workshop`/`canvas`,
  which have no member of their own in the SIGNED `ArtifactSource` enum -- see
  `packages/contracts/src/files.ts`'s own `FS1` note; the workaround mirrors F73's
  precedent of reusing `"interview"` for workshop rather than amending a signed contract).
- `apps/api/src/application/files/materialize-source.ts` -- the generic per-source
  materializer: one artifact + one version per `(sourceType, sourceRef)` call, same
  write-once / read-back-and-verify discipline as F04's `materializeArtifact` and F73's
  `materializeSessionFiles`, over the SAME `ArtifactRepository`/`ObjectStore` ports (no
  second storage path).
- `apps/api/src/domain/files/build-conversation-file.ts` -- assembles a conversation's
  messages into ONE `messages.jsonl` (R3's field list, snake_case on disk), proving the
  file-grain contract (V2): 50 messages -> 1 file, 50 lines.
- `apps/api/src/domain/files/canvas-mermaid.ts` -- minimal mermaid flowchart parse/render
  (3 node shapes: rectangle/rounded/diamond) + a structured-JSON layout snapshot builder,
  for D-08's round-trip assertion (V4).
- Three new test files (`tests/files/materialize-seven-sources.test.ts`,
  `tests/files/conversation-file-granularity.test.ts`,
  `tests/files/canvas-mermaid-roundtrip.test.ts`) -- pure vitest, in-memory
  `FakeArtifactRepository`/`FakeObjectStore` (reused from `tests/support/artifact-fakes.ts`,
  F73's own fakes), no Postgres dependency.

## Judgment calls / known gaps (see PR description for full detail)

1. `research` source's file names (`snapshot.html` + `citations.json`) are this feature's
   OWN table, distinct from the already-shipped `research-run` `ArtifactSource`'s existing
   plan (`run.json` + `citations.jsonl` in `domain/artifact/materialization.ts`). Not
   reconciled here -- changing a shipped feature's file names is that feature's own
   migration, not this one's.
2. `workshop`'s whiteboard photo is modelled as a single optional `whiteboard.jpg`; a real
   workshop may produce N photos. Out of this feature's 3-verification-command scope.
3. `sourceRef` is carried in the artifact `title` (`` `${sourceType}:${sourceRef}` ``), not
   a real `artifacts.source_ref` column -- no such column exists yet in the schema, and
   F73 already established the same workaround for its own session id. A real
   `GET /projects/:id/artifacts?source_ref=...` endpoint (V1's literal wording) is
   follow-up infra work, not built by this feature (which stays at the same "pure
   application logic over ports, no Postgres store yet" level F40 shipped at).
4. `canvas`/`workshop` reusing `"prototype-run"`/`"interview"` as their `ArtifactSource`
   tag is a documented workaround pending the FS1 signoff dispute already flagged in
   `packages/contracts/src/files.ts` (SIGNED `ArtifactSource` has 7 values; UC-22.3's own
   table needs `workshop` and `canvas` besides). This feature does not resolve FS1.
